# v0.24.9 — Cross-island bridge multi-sig and Merkle proof verification

## Operator user and CLI wallet hardening

- Created `/home/aitbc` as the `aitbc` operator home on `aitbc3` and `hub.aitbc`.
- Migrated CLI wallets from `/root/.aitbc/wallets` to `/home/aitbc/.aitbc/wallets`.
- Set wallet directory `0700` and wallet files `0600`.
- Updated `aitbc` user home to `/home/aitbc` (with a service restart on both nodes).
- Removed `/root/.aitbc/wallets` and left a note pointing operators to run `sudo -u aitbc aitbc <command>`.
- Documented the operator user / wallet locations in `AGENTS.md`.

- `cli/aitbc_cli/commands/wallet/basic.py`: `aitbc wallet balance <name>` now falls back to a local file wallet when the wallet daemon returns 404, so file-only wallets (e.g. `customer-wallet`, `shop-wallet`) can be queried.


- P2.4: automatic reinvestment from released escrow.
  - `aitbc ai submit --auto-reinvest-pct <pct>` creates an auto-stake order.
  - On escrow release the blockchain node stakes `pct%` of the payment for the provider.
  - Job status shows `reinvest_status: staked` and `reinvest_stake_id`.
  - Scenario docs: `docs/scenarios/40_auto_reinvestment.md`.
- Added `HUB_COORDINATOR_URL=http://hub.aitbc.bubuit.net/c/v1` to `/etc/aitbc/blockchain.env` on `aitbc3` and `hub.aitbc` so the `aitbc` operator user resolves the coordinator URL correctly without relying on a per-user `.aitbc.yaml`.
- Validated `sudo -u aitbc aitbc ai submit --payment 1.0 --provider-address 0xC10f0E4Fb1d162Bb27aF88A698b8C2e6E39A844F --model llama3.2:3b --prompt "What is 2+2?" --wait` on `hub.aitbc`: job completed, payment released, escrow tx `0x867529e7b692e222bb3406ec4b6ed51b86e8411da99654be14d962b38a913c74`.

- `aitbc-miner.service`: set `HOME=/var/lib/aitbc` so `ProtectHome=yes` does not break Whisper temp paths after the operator home move.
- `aitbc-pool-hub.service`: set `HOME=/var/lib/aitbc` and `PGSSLMODE=disable` so the hub pool-hub starts cleanly with the new `aitbc` home.
- Shop miner now registers and heartbeats with the hub pool-hub (`HUB_POOL_HUB_URL=http://hub.aitbc.bubuit.net/pool-hub`); `aitbc pool-hub status` on both nodes reports `miners_online: 1`.
- Disabled `aitbc-pool-hub.service` on `aitbc3` (shop/follower) and pointed the shop miner at the hub pool-hub.


- P2.5: Whisper, FFmpeg, and Ollama default shop offers.
  - `aitbc-miner` publishes default `whisper/base`, `ffmpeg/h264-transcode`, and
    `ollama/llama3.2:3b` software offers on startup and every 5 minutes by running
    the canonical `aitbc market offer` command.
  - `aitbc market offer` now works from shop nodes: it picks a wallet with a
    non-zero on-chain balance, falls back to the hub island (`ait-hub`), and
    registers the offer with the hub marketplace service.
  - Software-only marketplace listings no longer require a prior on-chain bond
    (hardware GPU bundles still do when `MARKET_BOND_MIN_AMOUNT` is set).
  - `aitbc market list` shows the default offers from the shop.
  - `aitbc market transcribe`, `aitbc market process`, and `aitbc market run`
    execute Whisper, FFmpeg, and Ollama jobs against the shop's public endpoints
    and release escrow on completion.
  - `apps/ffmpeg/main.py` maps consumer codec names (h264/hevc) to the correct
    FFmpeg encoders (`h264_nvenc`, etc.) and fixes bitrate/bufsize formatting.
  - `cli/aitbc_cli/commands/market/jobs.py` coerces `Decimal` costs to `float`
    before JSON and uses the offer's public endpoint for Ollama inference.
  - `examples/nginx/nginx-aitbc.conf.example` and `scripts/setup/install-nginx-node.sh`
    include `ffmpeg` and `whisper` upstream/location blocks on the correct ports.
  - Scenario docs: `docs/scenarios/41_whisper_ffmpeg_shop_offers.md` and
    `docs/scenarios/50_default_shop_offers.md`.
- Validated end-to-end ZK receipt verification: submitted `aitbc ai submit --wallet default --payment 1.0 --provider-address 0xC10f0E4Fb1d162Bb27aF88A698b8C2e6E39A844F --model llama3.2:3b --prompt "What is the capital of France?" --zk-proof-required --wait`; the completed receipt shows `zk_status: verified` and `aitbc zk verify --proof-id f714b502099b4813931d8594b9b57650` returns `verified: true, computation_correct: true, privacy_preserved: true`.


- P2.6: real IPFS daemon behind `aitbc ipfs`.
  - `aitbc ipfs upload|download|pin|list` now use the local Kubo HTTP API
    (`http://127.0.0.1:5001` by default, overridable with `IPFS_API_URL`).
  - Falls back to the filesystem stub when the daemon is not reachable.
  - Cross-node `aitbc ipfs download` validated over the public IPFS swarm
    from `aitbc3` to `hub.aitbc` and back.
  - `tests/cli/test_ipfs.py` updated to exercise the daemon-aware code path.
  - Scenario docs: `docs/scenarios/42_ipfs_daemon.md`.

- P2.7: compliance, plugins, and white-label expansion.
  - `aitbc brand` and `aitbc brand list` show active brand settings and available
    plugins.
  - `aitbc plugin list` and `aitbc plugin load` discover and load Python brand
    plugins from a configured directory.
  - `aitbc plugin create` now writes a `.py` file with `brand`, `roles`, and
    `identity_method` that `PluginManager` can load immediately, plus an optional
    manifest for documentation.
  - `aitbc compliance check` and `aitbc compliance classify` expose the policy
    engine without requiring a job submission.
  - `aitbc ai submit --compliance-framework <fw> --classification <label>`
    validates the label against the selected framework before submitting and
    attaches `data_classification` to the job constraints.
  - `whitelabel_demo.py` sample brand plugin under `plugins/`.
  - Lazily evaluated `get_active_brand()` in `wallet/staking.py` to avoid startup
    crashes when `AITBC_ACTIVE_PLUGIN` is set.
  - Scenario docs: `docs/scenarios/43_compliance_plugins_white_label.md`.
- Wired coordinator reputation into dispatch: `JobService` now loads `AgentReputation.trust_score` (0-1000, normalized to 0-1) when choosing the best miner, and `miner.py` records successful/failed job completions into the reputation service.
- `aitbc market list` now enriches offers with the canonical coordinator `trust_score` when the provider is a known agent, and the default sort prefers live trust score over marketplace avg_rating.

- Implemented P1.1: job completion records update `AgentReputation`; dispatch prefers `trust_score`; `aitbc market list` fetches and sorts by live reputation.


- Scenario 37: ZK high-value jobs.
  - Added `docs/scenarios/37_zk_high_value_jobs.md` documenting the P2.1 ZK
    receipt proof flow.
  - Live-validated on hub: payment 15 AIT inference job `324860acec664b5eac8fad85cc2cd873`
    completed with `zk_status`: `verified` and `zk_proof_id` set.
  - Linked from `docs/scenarios/README.md`.
- Registered `aitbc zk` CLI command (it existed but was not loaded in `core/main.py`).
- Validated scenario 37: `aitbc ai submit --payment 15 --zk-proof-required` produces a verified `zk_proof` in the receipt, releases escrow, and `aitbc zk verify --job-id` confirms `verified: true`.

- Registered missing CLI commands `aitbc auth` and `aitbc dashboard` in `core/main.py`.

- Fixed `aitbc auth login` URL normalization: strip trailing `/v1` from configured `coordinator_api_url` to avoid `/v1/v1/auth/nonce`.

- Updated scenario 34 (`docs/scenarios/34_hub_customer_node_e2e.md`) to v1.5, covering `aitbc auth login`, `aitbc dashboard`, `aitbc zk verify`, `aitbc reputation`, and trust-aware `aitbc market list`.

- `DatabaseConfig` now supports `DATABASE_URL`/`DATABASE_ADAPTER` for PostgreSQL without switching live SQLite deployments that only set `DATABASE_URL`.
- Removed the `AgentReputation.agent_id` foreign key to `ai_agent_workflows.id` so reputation profiles can be created for miners and other non-workflow agents.

- Hardened cross-chain bridge: reject same-chain locks, enforce `bridge_max_lock_amount`, and add a configurable `bridge_refund_delay_seconds` to prevent instant refunds.
